{"id": "EUVD-2026-102361", "enisaUuid": "53461c3d-b287-389e-878e-4729f8e43910", "description": "OpenSlide through 4.0.1 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the MIRAX reader that allows attackers to read past the slide_positions array via crafted Slidedat.ini values. Attackers can supply a MIRAX slide whose CameraImageDivisionsPerSide does not evenly divide the image counts, crashing applications that open it and corrupting tile geometry.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:16:55", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/openslide-mirax-slide-position-index-oob-read", "https://github.com/openslide/openslide/blob/fe79a9713bef2bfd64bbfefd15704060764b1274/src/openslide-vendor-mirax.c#L611-L635", "https://github.com/openslide/openslide/blob/fe79a9713bef2bfd64bbfefd15704060764b1274/src/openslide-vendor-mirax.c#L1033-L1034", "https://github.com/openslide/openslide", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openslide-through-4.0.1-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-mirax-get-tile-position"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5jq9-3x2q-j76q", "CVE-2026-111130"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9563eb51-12f9-39ae-ba8e-14a8fea37271", "product": {"name": "openslide", "vendor": {"name": "openslide"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5ec6dba9-f537-398d-b9de-627ff059ed11", "vendor": {"name": "openslide"}}], "isExploited": false}